{
  "moduleId": "m00204",
  "title": {
    "segmentId": "m00204:title:auto-1",
    "text": "Alcohols from Carbonyl Compounds: Grignard Reaction"
  },
  "documentClass": null,
  "metadata": {
    "uuid": "e3fbea5a-61cb-4095-a1c8-5acd1cb06bb6"
  },
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00001",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00001"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "R X reacts with magnesium to form Grignard reagent with formula R (delta negative) Mg (delta positive) X. Ketone reacts with Grignard, then hydronium to give alcohol with R."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00002",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00002"
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00003",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00003"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00002",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00002-alt",
          "text": "Cyclohexylmagnesium bromide reacts with formaldehyde to form cyclohexylmethanol. Phenylmagnesiumbromide reacts with 3-methylbutanal to form 3-methyl-1-phenyl-1-butanol. Ethylmagnesium bromide reacts with cyclohexanone to form 1-ethylcyclohexanol. Each requires ether solvent and hydronium workup."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_002.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00004",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00004"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00003",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00003-alt",
          "text": "Ethyl pentanoate reacts with two equivalents of methyl magnesium bromide, then hydronium ion to form 2-methyl-2-hexanol (tertiary alcohol, 85 percent yield) and ethanol."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_003.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00005",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00005"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00004",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00004-alt",
          "text": "An alkyl halide reacts with magnesium to form Grignard reagent. A carboxylic acid reacts with R Mg X in ether to form a carboxylic acid salt and R H."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_004.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00006",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00006"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00005",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00005-alt",
          "text": "A carboxylic acid reacts with tertiary butyl magnesium chloride and toluene to form an intermediate. This intermediate reacts with Turbo-Hauser base to form a ketone."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_TurboHaus.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00007",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00007"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00006",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00006-alt",
          "text": "A molecule connected to bromine and functional group. Grignard reagent is protonated by alcohol, amine, thiol, and carboxylic acid. It adds to aldehyde, ester, amide, nitrile, nitro and sulfonate group."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_005.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "id": "para-00008",
      "segmentId": "m00204:para:para-00008"
    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00007",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00204:alt:fig-00007-alt",
          "text": "A carbonyl compound (partial positive C, partial negative O) is attacked by R negative to form alkoxide intermediate. Hydronium workup converts this to alcohol."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_17_05_006.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
